  "result": "I fixed the queue in `src/queue.js` so it follows the contract. `npm test` passes with 5 of 5 tests, including three new regression tests in `test/queue.test.js`.\n\nThere were four bugs behind the three reports:\n- **Hang after a failure:** a rejected job never decremented `running`, so its slot stayed taken. The slot is now freed whether the job resolves or rejects.\n- **Jobs that throw or return a plain value:** `fn()` was assumed to return a promise. A synchronous throw or a non-promise return now works, and a throw rejects only that job's promise.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving early:** it only checked that nothing was pending. It now also requires that nothing is running.\n- **Single job after `pause()`/`resume()`:** `next()` started at most one job per call. It now loops until every free slot is filled.\n\nThe new tests cover:\n- a job that fails asynchronously, one that throws synchronously, and one that returns a plain value, with the queue carrying on afterwards;\n- `onIdle()` waiting for running jobs and resolving immediately on an empty queue;\n- `resume()` starting four jobs at once with concurrency 4 and never exceeding four.\n\nI didn't run the new tests against the original code, so I haven't confirmed that each one fails there.",
